The talk will give an overview on the ongoing crayfish virome research, including why invasive species are particularly interesting hosts to study, virus discovery, some of the challenges associated with host assignment in invertebrate virome studies, and a few specific case studies. For example, a reo-like virus, where they observed an association with histopathological changes.
